{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q15239768","formula":"C₆H₁₁NO₂","hill":"C6H11NO2","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":6.0,"H":11.0,"N":1.0,"O":2.0},"names":{"en":"Isonipecotic acid"},"descriptions":{"en":"Isonipecotic acid, also known as piperidine-4-carboxylic acid (P4C), is a conformationally constrained derivative of γ-aminobutyric acid (GABA) and a moderately potent GABAA receptor partial agonist. It consists of a piperidine ring with a carboxylic acid moiety in the iso position. The drug showed moderate-efficacy partial agonism of α1, α2, α3, and α5 subunit-containing GABAA receptors (EmaxTooltip maximal efficacy = 46–57%), but showed full or near-full agonism of α4 and α6 subunit-containing GABAA receptors (Emax = 83–104%)."},"fame":9,"pubchemCid":3773,"mass":129.16,"charge":0,"smiles":"C1CNCCC1C(=O)O","inchikey":"SRJOCJYGOFTFLH-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"piperidine-4-carboxylic acid","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"3773","atoms":20,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":2.38,"y":0.845,"z":-0.164,"el":"O"},{"x":1.59,"y":-1.202,"z":-0.781,"el":"O"},{"x":-2.209,"y":0.095,"z":-0.44,"el":"N"},{"x":0.409,"y":0.1,"z":0.883,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.56,"y":-1.08,"z":0.981,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.334,"y":1.389,"z":0.523,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.496,"y":-1.164,"z":-0.226,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.279,"y":1.201,"z":-0.665,"el":"C"},{"x":1.5,"y":-0.184,"z":-0.111,"el":"C"},{"x":0.902,"y":0.218,"z":1.856,"el":"H"},{"x":-1.167,"y":-0.962,"z":1.889,"el":"H"},{"x":-0.018,"y":-2.027,"z":1.091,"el":"H"},{"x":0.358,"y":2.211,"z":0.308,"el":"H"},{"x":-0.924,"y":1.705,"z":1.394,"el":"H"},{"x":-0.951,"y":-1.447,"z":-1.133,"el":"H"},{"x":-2.232,"y":-1.955,"z":-0.046,"el":"H"},{"x":-1.855,"y":2.122,"z":-0.809,"el":"H"},{"x":-0.709,"y":1.036,"z":-1.587,"el":"H"},{"x":-2.821,"y":0.001,"z":-1.25,"el